data: {"level":1,"reviewed":{"level":1,"label":"concept","text":"Welch's test compares two means without assuming the groups share a variance. Each group contributes its\nown variance of the mean, `var / n`, and the standard error is the square root of their sum. The degrees of\nfreedom are not `n_a + n_b − 2`. They come from matching the sum of the two terms to a scaled chi-square\n(the Welch–Satterthwaite approximation)."},"hints_note":null}

